Decision: keep one private bounded write-ahead log per active request, use a strict private format, and compact it at every durable message boundary.
Reason: stream-only UI state disappears on process death; append-before-display preserves it, while rejecting unknown fields is safe because this ephemeral private format quarantines only its own log and never blocks the authoritative session.
Capacity: 32 Agent streams + 8 subagents + 64 gateway runs + 64 scheduler runs = 168, below the single 256-log authority. Each session is limited to 4 logs, each log to 32 MiB, each record to 8 MiB, and discovery to 4,096 entries.
